  simulationStarted: "The mobile crane will test the crossing. Watch how the roadway and supporting members carry its load."
  liveLoadStarted: "The crane's weight is reaching the bridge. Check how the connected members share the load."
  vehicleEnteredBridge: "The crane is entering the bridge. Watch for overloaded members and a continuous roadway."
  vehicleReachedMidpoint: "The crane is near the middle. Look for members using a large share of their capacity."
  vehicleApproachingEnd: "The crane is approaching the far bank. Keep observing until it has completely crossed."
  highStressDetected: "Orange or red members are using a large share of their capacity. Inspect their supports and connections."
  stressLimitExceeded: "The bridge exceeded the contract's allowed stress. Locate the overloaded area before changing the design."
  firstMemberBreak: "A member failed. Note where the first break occurred and how the remaining members carry the load."
  vehicleStuck: "The crane has stopped moving. Check the roadway alignment, clearance, and connections."
  vehicleFailed: "The crane could not finish the crossing. Examine the failed area and the load path before testing again."
  bridgeSucceeded: "The crane reached the far bank. The bridge carried the required live load through the full crossing."
  simulationStopped: "Simulation stopped. Review the test results before deciding what to change."
